1 … rather than the false statement of law disclaiming such authority — within sixty (60) days of this Court's order, with any subsequent determination resting on the proper exercise of prosecutorial discretion rather than on a disclaimer of statutory authority","line":17,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-2-1-1-8ebd9e1d","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page":41,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"2","text":"Minn. Stat. §§ 8.31, 8.32 and 299C.061","n":"1","kind":"statute","target_doc":"MN-Stat-ch-8","target_page":"7","target_page_end":"8","target_pin":"§ 8.31, subd. 1","status":"mapped","target_quote":"The attorney general shall investigate violations of the law of this state respecting unfair, discriminatory, and other unlawful practices in business, commerce, or trade, and specifically, but not exclusively … the Prevention of Consumer Fraud Act (sections 325F.68 to 325F.70)","line":18,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-2-1-1-c6cc8e69","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page_end":8,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"2","text":"Minn. Stat. §§ 8.31, 8.32 and 299C.061","n":"1","kind":"statute","target_doc":"MN-Stat-ch-8","target_page":"10","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"§ 8.32, subd. 2(1)","status":"mapped","target_quote":"The attorney general shall: (1) enforce the provisions of law relating to consumer fraud and unlawful practices in connection therewith as set forth in sections 325F.68 and 325F.69","line":19,"k":2,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-2-1-2-c6cc8e69","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page":10,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"2","text":"Minn. Stat. §§ 8.31, 8.32 and 299C.061","n":"1","kind":"statute","target_doc":"MN-Stat-299C.061","target_page":"2","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"§ 299C.061, subd. 4(c)","status":"mapped","target_quote":"Notwithstanding paragraph (b), this section has no effect on the authority of the attorney general to investigate and enforce violations or suspected violations of Minnesota civil or criminal law.","line":20,"k":3,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-2-1-3-c6cc8e69","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page":2,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"3","text":"ECF No. 27 at 5–7","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"MN2594-027","target_page":"5","target_page_end":"7","target_pin":"Order at 5–7","status":"mapped","target_quote":"any federal constitutional injury was complete at the time Kirchner received the letter from the Attorney General's Office","line":21,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-3-1-1-cadda939","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":3,"target_pdf_page":5,"target_pdf_page_end":7,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"3","text":"Pennhurst State School & Hospital v. Halderman, 465 U.S. 89 (1984)","n":"1","kind":"case","target_doc":"1984 - Pennhurst v. Halderman, 465 U.S. 89","target_page":"","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"","status":"mapped","target_quote":"","line":22,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-3-1-1-65e6f713","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":null,"src_pdf_page":3,"target_pdf_page":null,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"3","text":"ECF No. 27 at 6, 8","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"MN2594-027","target_page":"6","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Order at 6","status":"mapped","target_quote":"Rather, he alleges an ongoing violation of state law","line":23,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-3-1-1-13cbddc2","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":3,"target_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"3","text":"ECF No. 27 at 6, 8","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"MN2594-027","target_page":"8","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Order at 8","status":"mapped","target_quote":"The complaint (ECF No. 1) is DISMISSED.","line":24,"k":2,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-3-1-2-13cbddc2","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":3,"target_pdf_page":8,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"3","text":"ECF No. 28","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"MN2594-028","target_page":"1","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Doc. 28","status":"mapped","target_quote":"The complaint (ECF No. 1) is DISMISSED.","line":25,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-3-1-1-3bee5179","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":3,"target_pdf_page":1,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"3","text":"ECF No. 27 at 8 n.2","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"MN2594-027","target_page":"8","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Order at 8","status":"mapped","target_quote":"Because Kirchner already had a chance to press his claims in Kirchner I, and because Kirchner has not explained how he would fix his deficient complaint now for a third time, his request is denied.","line":26,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-3-1-1-9fde99c8","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":3,"target_pdf_page":8,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"3","text":"ECF No. 27 at 4 n.1","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"MN2594-027","target_page":"4","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Order at 4","status":"mapped","target_quote":"Kirchner's motion for leave to file a sur-reply is therefore denied.","line":27,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-3-1-1-6bcbe54a","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":3,"target_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"3","text":"28 U.S.C. § 1915(a)(3)","n":"1","kind":"statute","target_doc":"usc-28-judiciary-and-judicial-procedure","target_page":"","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"§ 1915(a)(3)","status":"mapped","target_quote":"An appeal may not be taken in forma pauperis if the trial court certifies in writing that it is not taken in good faith.","line":28,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-3-1-1-cba433a6","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":3,"target_pdf_page":830,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":{"pdf":830,"by":"section","key":"1915","file":"usc28@119-111.pdf"},"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"3","text":"Coppedge v. United States, 369 U.S. 438, 445","n":"1","kind":"case","target_doc":"1962 - Coppedge v. United States, 369 U.S. 438","target_page":"445","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"445","status":"mapped","target_quote":"We consider a defendant's good faith in this type of case demonstrated when he seeks appellate review of any issue not frivolous.","line":29,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-3-1-1-0608f85b","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":3,"target_pdf_page":8,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"3","text":"No. 0:26-cv-00726-PJS-ECW; Eighth Circuit No. 26-1615","n":"1","kind":"docket","target_doc":"","target_page":"","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Kirchner I and its appeal","status":"unresolved","target_quote":"","line":30,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-3-1-1-824ff434","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":null,"src_pdf_page":3,"target_pdf_page":null,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":false,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"3","text":"Federal Rule of Appellate Procedure 24(c)","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Federal Rules of Appellate Procedure (Dec. 1, 2025, official pamphlet, GPO print CPRT-119HPRT61919 via govinfo.gov)","target_page":"25","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Rule 24(c)","status":"mapped","target_quote":"A party allowed to proceed on appeal in forma pauperis may request that the appeal be heard on the original record without reproducing any part.","line":31,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-3-1-1-4c3545ff","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":3,"target_pdf_page":40,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"4","text":"Rule 24(a)(2)","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Federal Rules of Appellate Procedure (Dec. 1, 2025, official pamphlet, GPO print CPRT-119HPRT61919 via govinfo.gov)","target_page":"25","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Rule 24(a)(2)","status":"mapped","target_quote":"If the district court grants the motion, the party may proceed on appeal without prepaying or giving security for fees and costs, unless a statute provides otherwise. If the district court denies the motion, it must state its reasons in writing.","line":32,"k":1,"unit_id":"MN2594-035-4-1-1-e15452fc","violations":[],"warnings":[],"target_ligature_drop":false,"src_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page":40,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"MN2594-035","src_page":"4","text":"Rule 24(a)(5)","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Federal Rules of Appellate Procedure (Dec. 1, 2025, official pamphlet, GPO print CPRT-119HPRT61919 via govinfo.gov)","target_pa